claim.claim-text:
receiving video data which is arranged in a plurality of luma subblocks and a plurality of chroma subblocks, wherein the video data has a color sampling format, and each chroma subblock corresponds to one or more luma subblocks according to the color sampling format;
deriving an affine motion vector for a chroma subblock out of the chroma subblocks using an average luma motion vector obtained by averaging motion vectors of the corresponding luma subblocks; and
predicting the chroma subblock based on the derived affine motion vector;
wherein the corresponding luma subblocks are derived according to the color sampling format;
characterised in that
the averaging process uses the motion vectors from different luma subblocks under different color sampling formats, wherein in the case that the color sampling format is 4:4:4, the average luma motion vector is the motion vector of one corresponding luma subblock, wherein indices of the one corresponding luma subblock are the same as indices of the chroma subblock, the indices comprises a horizontal index and a vertical index, and in the case that the color sampling format is 4:2:2, the average luma motion vector is obtained by taking an average of the motion vectors of two corresponding luma subblocks, wherein vertical indices of the two corresponding luma subblocks are the same as a vertical index of the chroma subblock.

deriving an affine motion vector for a luma subblock out of the luma subblocks using a control point based affine motion model;
invoking a rounding process with the affine motion vectors of the corresponding luma subblocks, rightShift set equal to 7, and leftShift set equal to 0 as inputs;
wherein the average luma motion vector is derived using the rounded motion vectors.

left shifting the motion vectors of control points of the luma subblocks by 7 to obtain left shifted luma motion vectors;
left shifting the differences between affine parameters by 7 and then dividing left shifted differences between affine parameters by the block width or height to obtain left shifted and divided differences between affine parameters, wherein the differences between affine parameters are the difference between motion vectors of top-right control point and top-left control point and the difference between motion vectors of bottom-left control point and the top-left control point;
deriving the affine motion vector for the luma subblock out of the luma subblocks using a control point based affine motion model, based on the left shifted luma motion vectors and the left shifted and divided differences between affine parameters.

a processor; and
a memory configured to store instructions executable by the processor;
wherein the processor, upon execution of the instructions, is configured to:
receive video data which is arranged in a plurality of luma subblocks and a plurality of chroma subblocks, wherein the video data has a color sampling format, and each chroma subblock corresponds to one or more luma subblocks according to the color sampling format; and
derive an affine motion vector for a chroma subblock out of the chroma subblocks using an average luma motion vector obtained by averaging motion vectors of the corresponding luma subblocks; and
predict the chroma subblock based on the derived affine motion vector;
wherein the corresponding luma subblocks are derived according to the color sampling format;

derive an affine motion vector for a luma subblock out of the luma subblocks using a control point based affine motion model;
invoke a rounding process with the affine motion vectors of the corresponding luma subblocks, rightShift set equal to 7, and leftShift set equal to 0 as inputs;
wherein the average luma motion vector is derived using the rounded motion vectors.

left shift the motion vectors of control points of the luma subblocks by 7 to obtain left shifted luma motion vectors;
left shift the differences between affine parameters by 7 and then divide left shifted differences between affine parameters by the block width or height to obtain the left shifted and divided differences between affine parameters, wherein the differences between affine parameters are the difference between motion vectors of top-right control point and top-left control point and the difference between motion vectors of bottom-left control point and the top-left control point;
deriving the affine motion vector for the luma subblock out of the luma subblocks using a control point based affine motion model, based on the left shifted luma motion vectors and the left shifted and divided differences between affine parameters;
wherein the motion vectors of the corresponding luma subblocks are derived using the higher precision luma motion vectors.
